   10. Respectful Slopping -- Attribution and Automated Tools.

       Paragraphs (a) through (e) are conditions of the copyright permission
       granted in Section 2, additional to Section 4. They apply to the reuse
       of protected material for which that permission is required.
       Paragraph (f) is a community request only.

       (a) Credit with reused material. When You incorporate copyrightable
           portions of the Work into another project under this License,
           including a project used only internally, You must include a
           clear attribution notice in the corresponding Source form.
           The notice must identify the originating project by its stated
           name and canonical project URL, or by the other source identifier
           supplied with the Work if no URL is supplied; identify the
           material to which the notice applies; and accurately state
           whether it was copied, adapted, or translated. Include an
           original file, symbol, or revision reference when supplied with
           the material and reasonably available.

           Preserve applicable upstream copyright, license, and attribution
           notices. Credit for Your modifications may be added alongside
           that credit. Describing copied or adapted material merely as
           "inspired by" does not satisfy this paragraph.

       (b) Placement. Put the notice in a comment adjacent to the reused
           material or in a file header that clearly identifies the affected
           material. One notice may cover multiple portions in the same
           file if its scope is clear. If the format does not support
           comments, put the notice in an accompanying attribution file
           identifying the relevant file and material. An existing notice
           satisfying these requirements need not be duplicated.

           An unchanged copy of the Work retained as a separate package or
           directory may instead carry one accompanying notice identifying
           that package or directory, provided the applicable original
           notices remain intact. Portions extracted from that copy into
           other files require the comments or accompanying attribution
           described above.

       (c) Automated assistance. These requirements apply equally when You
           reuse the Work with an artificial-intelligence model, coding
           agent, code generator, or other automated tool. You remain
           responsible for compliance in material You incorporate or
           distribute under this License. An AI-generated label does not
           replace attribution. Changing identifiers, formatting, or
           programming languages does not remove this requirement where
           protected material from the Work remains.

       (d) Distribution. Preserve the required attribution in Source
           distributions. When distributing Object form, including
           mechanically generated or minified output from which comments
           have been removed, include the corresponding attribution in an
           accompanying NOTICE file, third-party notices document, or other
           customary documentation delivered with that distribution.
           Section 4's license-copy and notice requirements also apply.
           This section does not require public release of Source form,
           advertising credit, or attribution in an application's ordinary
           user interface.

       (e) Accuracy and scope. Attribution must be accurate and must not
           imply endorsement by the originating project or its contributors.
           This section imposes no condition on uses that do not require
           permission under this License, including independent creation,
           reuse of unprotected ideas or conventional techniques, and uses
           permitted by applicable exceptions or limitations to copyright.
           It does not require speculation about unidentified sources in a
           model's training data. Required attribution for identifiable
           reused material remains applicable.

       (f) Known inspiration -- community request. When a project-specific
           idea, design, or approach from the Work knowingly and materially
           informs an independent implementation, please include an
           "Inspired by" comment naming and linking to the project and
           identifying the particular idea or approach borrowed. For a
           file that cannot contain comments, use an accompanying
           attribution file. This paragraph is a nonbinding request;
           it does not extend copyright protection to ideas or impose
           conditions on rights You already possess.

