APPENDIX: Applying this draft and guiding coding agents

This appendix provides application guidance and examples. It does not add
license conditions.

1. Identify the project.

   Put the license text above in your repository's LICENSE file. Identify
   your project, canonical URL, and copyright holder in your README or
   NOTICE and in source headers where practical. Replace the bracketed
   placeholders below with actual values; do not leave the brackets.

   This is a custom draft. The LicenseRef below is a locally defined
   reference, not an official SPDX-listed license identifier or a statement
   of OSI approval. Provide the full corresponding license text.

   Suggested source header, using the language's comment syntax:

     Copyright [YEAR] [COPYRIGHT HOLDER]
     SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Respectful-Slop-1.0-Draft
     Project: [PROJECT NAME]
     Source: [CANONICAL PROJECT URL]
     License text: [URL OR RELATIVE PATH TO LICENSE]

2. Suggested NOTICE content.

     [PROJECT NAME]
     [CANONICAL PROJECT URL]
     Copyright [YEAR] [COPYRIGHT HOLDER]

     Licensed under the Respectful Slop License, Version 1.0-Draft.
     The complete terms appear in LICENSE.

   Keep NOTICE factual. Operative obligations belong in the license text.

3. Attribution for copied or adapted material.

   Example for a copied portion:

     // Copied from [PROJECT NAME]: [CANONICAL PROJECT URL]
     // Applies to: [FUNCTION, TYPE, OR BLOCK]
     // Original source: [FILE OR SYMBOL, AND REVISION IF AVAILABLE]
     // Copyright [YEAR] [UPSTREAM COPYRIGHT HOLDER]
     // This portion: Respectful Slop License 1.0-Draft; see [LICENSE PATH].

   Example for a modified portion:

     // Adapted from [PROJECT NAME]: [CANONICAL PROJECT URL]
     // Applies to: [FUNCTION, TYPE, OR BLOCK]
     // Original source: [FILE OR SYMBOL, AND REVISION IF AVAILABLE]
     // Changes: [BRIEF DESCRIPTION OF YOUR CHANGES]
     // Copyright [YEAR] [UPSTREAM COPYRIGHT HOLDER]
     // This portion: Respectful Slop License 1.0-Draft; see [LICENSE PATH].

   Preserve any other applicable upstream notices. A short credit comment
   does not replace the obligation to supply the license on distribution.
   In a file containing material under multiple licenses, identify the
   affected portions accurately.

4. Attribution for a separately implemented idea.

     // Inspired by [PROJECT NAME]: [CANONICAL PROJECT URL]
     // Borrowed approach: [SPECIFIC IDEA OR DESIGN].
     // Implemented independently.

   Use "implemented independently" only when accurate. If protected code or
   other expression was actually copied or adapted, use the appropriate
   attribution and comply with the applicable license.

5. Suggested AGENTS.md guidance.

   Merge the following into the project's existing agent instructions.
   These are workflow instructions and do not independently create a
   license obligation over unprotected ideas.

   Respectful slopping

   When copying, adapting, or translating code from this project, preserve
   its license and applicable upstream notices. Add a nearby "Copied from",
   "Adapted from", or "Translated from" comment naming the project, linking
   to its canonical URL, and identifying the affected material.

   When deliberately borrowing a project-specific idea, design, or approach,
   add an "Inspired by" comment naming the project, linking to it, and
   describing the particular idea borrowed.

   Use the project identity and canonical URL supplied by the repository.
   Include the original file or revision when known. Record changes to
   copied material. For formats without comments, use a companion
   attribution file that maps the credit to the affected material.

   Do not label copied or adapted code merely "inspired by". Do not invent
   sources, remove applicable upstream credit, or imply endorsement.
   Preserve the required notices in distributed source and binary packages.

   Slop respectfully. Keep the credit attached.

6. Drafting status and adoption notes.

   This draft changes the license's name, version, License definition,
   and application examples, and adds Section 10. Sections 2 through 9
   retain the base text. The additional requirements should be reviewed
   as part of the complete custom license; approval or compatibility
   conclusions for the original license do not automatically apply.

   This draft has not been reviewed by a lawyer or submitted for OSI
   approval. Have qualified software/IP counsel review it before adopting
   it as a project's governing license, especially if mandatory credit for
   independently implemented ideas is important to your intended terms.

   Apply this license only to material you own or have authority to license
   under these terms. Do not replace the notices or licenses of third-party
   material. Earlier grants under another license are not withdrawn by
   publishing this draft.

   Under U.S. copyright law, ideas, algorithms, program logic, systems, and
   methods are not themselves protected by copyright. That is why Section
   10(f) states an inspiration-credit norm and the agent instructions turn
   it into an explicit project workflow. A separate binding promise about
   pure ideas would require separate contract analysis.

